peck:
A minute to smile and an hour to weep in,
A pint of joy to a peck of trouble,
And never a laugh but the moans come double;

peckahwood:
Shoutin' hallelujah.
Peckahwood erpon de tree
Tappin' lak a hammah;

pecker:
In orchards near and far away
The grey wood-pecker taps and bores;
The men are merry at their chores,

pecks:
Why else do these things move him, leaf or stone?
The bird’s not moved, that pecks at a spring-shoot;
Nor yet the horse, before a quarry, a-graze:

You are a rose, but set with sharpest spine;
You are a pretty bird that pecks at me;
You are a little squirrel on a tree,
